INSERT INTO "experiments" VALUES(1,'What code and runtime evidence explains when a Hyland officer clone changes ActiveSelf during NPC.EnterBuilding, and does it relate to the NPC.GetAndValidateReferences throw hypothesis for OfficerLee2 (unknown #2)?','Test run 3 (mod_build=0a7651c, general profile, 776 events, 22 errors, NEEDS_ATTENTION) shows OfficerLee2 completing NPC.EnterBuilding cleanly (ActiveSelf stayed True throughout, IsInBuilding False->True). ~45ms later CLONE ROOT SETACTIVE fires with RequestedActive=False, driving ActiveSelf True->False on the same clone. The new CloneRootSetActivePatch Harmony prefix captured a stack trace at this first deactivation (Instance=-376250), but it only shows System.Environment.get_StackTrace() -> CloneRootSetActivePatch.Prefix -> DMD<GameObject::SetActive> -> the native il2cpp trampoline -- it terminates at the IL2CPP managed/native boundary and does not reveal the actual game-code caller. This stack-capture approach cannot answer the question as designed. Separately, and directly relevant to unknown #2: this run''s 22 errors contain ZERO occurrences of NPC.GetAndValidateReferences -- the specific throw named in the hypothesis (a vs b) did not reproduce at all in this run, so neither hypothesis was tested. All 22 errors are instead unrelated NullReferenceException in ScheduleOne.NPCs.NPC.get_ID() called from Geraldine.Awake(), occurring during CartelGoon.NPC.Awake for 5 goon instances (1277312/14/16/18/20). The mod''s own GOON LIFECYCLE logging shows this is already captured (CaptureError=...) and self-heals -- the After= snapshot shows each goon fully initialized (NPCID=cartelgoon, HealthAlive=True) moments later. This is a distinct, non-blocking, already-handled race in goon Awake ordering, not the OfficerLee2 GetAndValidateReferences blocker.',6,3,'0a7651c-dirty','2026-09-09T01:59:30.118Z');
INSERT INTO "experiments" VALUES(2,'What code and runtime evidence explains when a Hyland officer clone changes ActiveSelf during NPC.EnterBuilding? (follow-up to experiment #1, whose GameObject.SetActive-level stack trace terminated at the IL2CPP native boundary and could not identify the actual caller.)','Test run 4 (mod_build=fd59a48-dirty, general profile, 860 events, 23 errors, NEEDS_ATTENTION) used new FishNet-level instrumentation (NetworkObjectTryStartDeactivationPatch on NetworkObject.TryStartDeactivation, added this build) to trace past the earlier IL2CPP boundary. Result: OfficerLee2 completes the local (non-RPC) EnterBuilding overload cleanly (event #1334/#1336, ActiveSelf stays True), passes one PoliceStation.Update tick with no change (#1345/#1346), then ~4ms later NetworkObject.TryStartDeactivation is called on it directly: event #1347 (BEFORE) shows ActiveSelf=True, ActiveHierarchy=True, IsSpawned=False, ServerInitialized=False, ClientInitialized=False; event #1351 (AFTER, 1ms later) shows ActiveSelf=False, ActiveHierarchy=False. This directly identifies FishNet''s own NetworkObject.TryStartDeactivation as the caller that deactivates the clone root -- not arbitrary game code, and not reachable from the earlier GameObject.SetActive-level Harmony prefix because the call originates inside FishNet''s native-adjacent lifecycle handling, past where the IL2CPP-truncated stack trace could see. Separately, this build''s own automated-testing changes (AutomaticSaveCreator native save create/overwrite, TestSessionManager auto-quit) were also verified working end-to-end in this same session via TestResults/20260909T143458Z-2688/events.jsonl: save_create_requested -> save_create_slot_selected (SlotIndex=4, overwrite=True) -> save_create_overwrite_confirmed -> save_create_started -> character_creation_completed (t+78s) -> test_session_auto_quit (t+125s), with an empty errors.jsonl for the whole session.',7,4,'fd59a48-dirty','2026-09-09T14:43:59.442Z');
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(1,2,NULL,'OfficerLee2''s copied SceneId maps back to OfficerLee, ruling out a genuinely independent disposable SWAT clone.','strong','active',1,NULL,262,'2026-09-08T03:41:22.493Z','2026-09-08T03:41:22.493Z',NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(2,NULL,NULL,'Run 2 was a short ''general'' profile session (menu load/mod init only, 151 lines) and is not comparable in coverage to Run 1''s long ''read-only-audit'' session (350 event rows, 18 tagged officers). The near-total event/entity diff between runs 1 and 2 reflects session scope, not a regression.','confirmed','active',NULL,2,NULL,'2026-09-08T06:07:43.206Z','2026-09-08T06:07:43.206Z',NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(3,NULL,NULL,'Vanilla police manpower is a finite, per-station pool: PoliceStation.OfficerPool (serialized List<PoliceOfficer>). LawManager.StartFootpatrol/StartVehiclePatrol and PoliceStation.Dispatch only ever call PoliceStation.PullOfficer() to draw from that pool; none construct, Instantiate, or FishNet-spawn a PoliceOfficer. Confirmed via Cpp2IL RVA-level static analysis against the local GameAssembly.dll build (MVID 7DE71175-5AAF-4970-83D4-77858937A8B5), not just IL2CPP metadata stubs. Source: HylandHeat repo docs/POLICE_MANPOWER_RESEARCH.md.','strong','active',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-08T19:34:20.507Z','2026-09-08T19:34:20.507Z',NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(4,1,NULL,'A dead PoliceOfficer is never destroyed, cloned, or returned to its station OfficerPool by NPCHealth.Die(). It only sets IsDead/zeroes Health and fires death events; it does not call PoliceOfficer.Deactivate() or NPC.EnterBuilding(). PoliceOfficer.CheckDeactivation() (which leads to the pool-return path) requires the officer to be conscious, so a dead officer cannot recycle through that path while dead. This is the confirmed mechanism behind the observed "kill enough police and the rest of the day gets safer" effect. Generic revival exists (NPCHealth.Revive(), gated on the police NPCData.Health preset having CanRevive=true, an unconfirmed asset value) but even a revived officer must still complete the normal deactivate/return path before becoming available again. Source: HylandHeat repo docs/POLICE_MANPOWER_RESEARCH.md.','strong','active',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-08T19:34:20.687Z','2026-09-08T19:34:20.687Z',NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(5,2,NULL,'An inactive OfficerLee2 clone (independent NPCDataObject id=officerlee2, fresh BakedGUID, all clone-local references confirmed non-null pre-activation) throws during NPC.GetAndValidateReferences -> NPC.Awake -> PoliceOfficer.Awake on its first activation. Post-failure state: activeSelf=true, NPCManager.NPCRegistry unchanged (Lee2 still absent), NPCData is null, NPCManager.GetNPC("officerlee2") returns null. Cpp2IL RVA-level re-audit of GetAndValidateReferences (0x87FC80) shows it makes 5 same-GameObject GetComponent<T>() calls (NPCInventory, NPCHealth, EntityVisibility, NPCMovement, NetworkedEquipper) then 6 parameterless GetComponentInChildren<T>() calls (DialogueHandler, Avatar, NPCAwareness, NPCResponses, NPCActions, NPCBehaviour, plus VOEmitter under Avatar.HeadBone) -- the parameterless overload excludes inactive descendants. This is the confirmed blocker for officer-clone-based reinforcement, the mod''s stated next major feature. Source: HylandHeat repo HylandHeat/Docs/Research/OFFICER_CLONE_BLOCKER_SUMMARY_2.md.','strong','superseded',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-08T19:34:42.937Z','2026-09-09T04:08:14.490Z',7);
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(6,NULL,'CartelGoon','CartelGoon.NPC.Awake throws a captured, self-healing NullReferenceException on every observed goon spawn. Test run 3 shows it for all 5 spawned goons (UnityInstance 1277312/14/16/18/20): the exception originates in ScheduleOne.NPCs.NPC.get_ID(), called from ScheduleOne.NPCs.CharacterClasses.Geraldine.Awake() -- Geraldine is a template/base NPC character class whose Awake() runs as part of CartelGoon''s own Awake chain before CartelGoon-specific identity fields are set, so get_ID() is reached before NPCID is assigned. The mod''s own GOON LIFECYCLE BEFORE/AFTER logging already captures this (CaptureError=Il2CppException:...) rather than crashing, and the AFTER snapshot taken moments later shows each goon fully initialized (NPCID=cartelgoon, HealthAlive=True, InSpawnedList as expected) -- so the goon self-heals and this does not currently block spawning. Distinct from, and not a cause of, the unrelated NPC.GetAndValidateReferences throw investigated for OfficerLee2 in unknown #2/experiment #1.','strong','active',6,3,NULL,'2026-09-09T03:13:00.444Z','2026-09-09T03:13:00.444Z',NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" VALUES(7,2,NULL,'Finding #5''s documented first-activation throw for OfficerLee2 does not reproduce in test run 3 (mod_build=0a7651c) and is superseded. HylandHeat repo doc OFFICER_CLONE_GETANDVALIDATE_REAUDIT.md (dated 2026-09-07, newer than finding #5''s cited source OFFICER_CLONE_BLOCKER_SUMMARY_2.md from 2026-09-02) documents a readiness fix already present in the code at commit 22ab44d (an ancestor of 0a7651c): the readiness source now prefers the cached PoliceOfficer.Avatar reference and falls back to GetComponentInChildren<Avatar>(true), and the clone factory explicitly enables the cloned Avatar GameObject before root activation when needed. Test run 3''s own captured events directly confirm this fix working end-to-end for OfficerLee2, not just for the doc''s Jackson/Lee readiness-queue case: event #497 shows the inactive clone created (HasPoliceOfficer=True); events #501-#550 (the exact same-GameObject/child lookup dump called for as ''test 1'' in OFFICER_CLONE_BLOCKER_SUMMARY_2.md) show all required components -- NPCInventory, NPCHealth, NPCMovement, NetworkedEquipper, EntityVisibility (same-GameObject) and DialogueHandler, Avatar, NPCAwareness, NPCResponses, NPCActions, NPCBehaviour, VOEmitter (child) -- found=True, Clone=True/CloneLocal=True; event #552 shows CLONE ROOT SETACTIVE succeeding (RequestedActive=True, ActiveSelf=True) with no throw; event #553 confirms AvatarHierarchyFound=True post-activation; events #555-#559 show OfficerLee2 successfully admitted to the Police station (Pool=0->1, ContainsClone=True, IsInBuilding=True); event #560 shows it counted in OFFICER CLONE QUEUE PROGRESS as ExistingManagedCloneCount=1. This confirms Hjarni''s narrative (Lee2 completes Awake/registration; remaining behavior of interest is the later ActiveSelf=False after station admission, already captured separately in experiment #1) and contradicts finding #5''s failure-state description, which reflected an earlier build predating this fix.','strong','active',6,3,NULL,'2026-09-09T03:41:21.783Z','2026-09-09T03:41:21.783Z',NULL);
INSERT INTO "relationships" VALUES(1,2,'IS_CLONE_OF',1,1,NULL,'Matched SceneId; see finding 1','2026-09-08T04:42:17.409Z');
